<title>USA: Fonda Group sells $120 mln in 144A notes.</title>
<headline>Fonda Group sells $120 mln in 144A notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue from The Fonda Group Inc was priced in the 144A private placement market on Monday, according to lead manager Bear Stearns &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>The deal was increased from an original $110 million to $120 million, according to sources.</p>
<p>BORROWER THE FONDA GROUP INC</p>
<p>AMT $120 MLN	 COUPON 9.50 PCT   MATURITY 3/1/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NOTES ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 9/1/1997 LAST MOODY'S B3    YIELD 9.50 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-MINUS   SPREAD 310 BPS    CALLABLE  NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1678</p>
